     3	// branch with fakes.
     4	//
     5	// The run key is the UTC date of the scheduled time (J15: Cloud Scheduler's retries carry the same scheduled time),
     6	// except a manual Force run, keyed by the day it actually runs (see runKey; DECISIONS #64).
     7	// Then, in order:
     8	//   1. Done already? Any COMPLETE folder weekly/<key>-*/ → "already done"; nothing is started.
     9	//   2. Running already? This database's operations, filtered to exports whose prefix is gs://<bucket>/weekly/<key>-:
    10	//      one not done → wait on it. One done SUCCESSFUL → its folder must now be complete ("already done"), else throw
    11	//      (inconsistent: a person looks). Ones that FAILED, were CANCELLED or carry an error are history: logged, never
    12	//      resumed, their prefixes never reused.
    13	//   3. Otherwise export to a fresh prefix weekly/<key>-<6 chars> and wait on it — unless less than START_RESERVE_MS of
    14	//      the budget is left, when it throws instead and the next retry starts it.
    15	// The budget is 1,500 s from the start of the run, and it bounds EVERY call to Google as well as the waiting (each call
    16	// gets only the time that's left, deadline.js), so the error and its alert always happen before Cloud Run's 1,800 s
    17	// kill; the next retry resumes at step 2. Success needs: done, no error, state SUCCESSFUL, the expected prefix, and
    18	// the complete folder visible in the bucket. Anything else throws.
    19	//
    20	// A rare duplicate (two runs racing, or a lost reply not yet listed) is a second COMPLETE copy in its own folder, never
    21	// a mixed one (Christie, O5). State is the bucket plus the operation list; there is no Firestore collection.
    22	'use strict';
